summary:
  A command left in the file by a crashed session is obeyed on the next start.

history:
  The command file outlives the session that wrote it, and the widget's only
  guard was "a number I have not seen" — after a restart it has seen none.
  A stop from yesterday then counted as new. The number is a moment, and an
  old moment is refused whatever it says.

target:
  package/contents/ui/MprisCommandGate.qml

find:
              if (isNaN(seq) || seq <= lastSeq || nowMs - seq > 10000) continue;

replace:
              if (isNaN(seq) || seq <= lastSeq) continue;

expect:
  Killed by test_invariants::test_a_command_older_than_ten_seconds_is_never_obeyed
  and by tests/qml/tst_mpriscommandgate.qml::test_a_line_older_than_ten_seconds_is_never_obeyed.
  Line-neutral.
